      "slug": "corner-increase",
      "term": "Corner increase",
      "definition": "Three dc worked into one corner stitch: 1 dc, then 2 dc into the same stitch, then 1 dc. The extra stitch turns the fabric at 90 degrees without curling."
    },
    {
      "slug": "fold-round",
      "term": "Fold round",
      "definition": "A round worked into the back loop only at the junction of base and sides. The unused front loops form a visible ridge that holds the sides upright."
    },
    {
      "slug": "weaving-in-ends",
      "term": "Weaving in ends",
      "definition": "Threading yarn tails through stitches with the tapestry needle."
    }
